hypotheses.statement:
Let $$K=\begin{pmatrix}A&C\\ B&D\end{pmatrix}\in\mathop{\mathrm{GL}}_{n+r}(\mathbb C),
 \qquad A\in\mathop{\mathrm{GL}}_n(\mathbb C),\quad D\in\mathop{\mathrm{GL}}_r(\mathbb C).$$ Write the action of $K$ as $(x,z_{\rm in})\mapsto(x',z_{\rm out})$. The map $(x,z_{\rm out})\mapsto(x',z_{\rm in})$ is the invertible matrix $$\label{pivot:eq:pivot-matrix}
 \widetilde K=
 \begin{pmatrix}
 A-CD^{-1}B&CD^{-1}\\
 -D^{-1}B&D^{-1}
 \end{pmatrix},
 \qquad p(\widetilde K)\le p(K)+4r.$$

Every invertible $2\times2$ matrix all of whose entries are nonzero has price at most $3/2$. In particular, $$\label{pivot:eq:pair-bound}
 p\left(\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\1&u\end{pmatrix}\right)
 \le\frac32\qquad (u\in\mathbb C\setminus\{0,1\}).$$

